<BaseLayout title="About">

  <div class="page">

    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      I am currently completing a PhD at the School of Public Health and Preventive Medicine at Monash University in Melbourne, Australia.
    </p>

    <p>
      My research focuses on advancing methods to optimise the impact and reduce waste of musculoskeletal health research. In particular, I am working on refining and validating the
      <a href="https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0281308" target="_blank">
        Australia and New Zealand Musculoskeletal Clinical Trials Network Research
        Question Importance Tool (ANZMUSC-RQIT)</a>,
        which helps prioritise research that matters most to patients, clinicians, and other stakeholders.
        This work is supported by the Australian government, Monash University, and ANZMUSC.
    </p>

    <p>
      Alongside my PhD, I contribute to Cochrane living systematic reviews that inform the
      <a href="https://livingguidelines.org" target="_blank">
        Australian Living Guidelines for the Pharmacological Management of Inflammatory Arthritis</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Outside of research, I enjoy the ocean (or wave pool), good coffee, running, discussing faith and beliefs, and spending time with family and friends.
    </p>

  </div>

</BaseLayout>
